 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409549 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409553 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409554 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "90260639-fefe-562c-8509-7dc58803f6c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409552 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409555 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c3c16b06-37a6-5eac-b3ba-318617c8302e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e7c2354d-85e6-577f-a722-6c718f129147" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132726" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})?$\n\n- Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(\\sqrt{3},1)$\n- ${f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})$ is defined\n- ${f}_{y}(0,1)$ is defined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a3b6388-98bd-5083-8d1c-f60a05890b23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409557 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{y} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(\\frac{x}{y})}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{x}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}+1}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(\\sqrt{3},1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{1})=\\frac{\\pi }{3},\n$$\n\nand both partial derivatives are also defined at $(\\sqrt{3},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =\\frac{1}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {f}_{y}(\\sqrt{3},1) & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}+{1}^{2}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3})$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,\\sqrt{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is also true. Indeed, the function $f$ itself is defined at $(0,1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(0,1)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{0}{1})=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(0,1)=-\\frac{0}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72010" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y)={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}?$\n\n- Both partial derivatives exist at the point $(1,-1)$\n- ${f}_{y}(-1,-1)$ is defined\n- ${f}_{x}(0,1)$ is defined" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "538fdcf0-8dcd-525c-becd-0317742dbf1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409558 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{y}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{y{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\cdot \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{xy}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}}{2\\sqrt{xy}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one. \n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(1,-1)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(1)(-1)}}=-{e}^{\\sqrt{-1}}\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have a negative number under the radical.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the function $f$ is defined at $(-1,-1)$, where we have \n\n$$\nf(-1,-1)={e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}={e}^{\\sqrt{1}}={e}^{1}=e,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(-1,-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-1,-1) & =\\frac{(-1){e}^{\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}}{2\\sqrt{(-1)(-1)}}=-\\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{1}}}{2\\sqrt{1}}=-\\frac{e}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we substitute $(0,1)$ into ${f}_{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n{f}_{x}(0,1)=1\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}}{2\\sqrt{0\\cdot 1}}=\\frac{{e}^{0}}{2\\sqrt{0}}=\\frac{1}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined since we have division by zero.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II  only'." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132654" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{1}{z},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5744243e-c58b-5537-916f-bee0cb473253" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409559 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xyz)$ is defined only when $xyz>0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x}$ is defined only when $x\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\n- The function $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{1}{z}$ is defined only when $z\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivatives of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xyz>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409563 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "06a4b700-aa67-595f-ad77-c3a9c2d08fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409560 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1786d23c-6b2b-5b25-8a34-a3df54af58bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409561 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "488b6ab6-cae5-5979-9b52-c3723c3f093b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409562 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186335822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61817e36-5704-54ae-b054-a7bf550b56c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409563 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "be87cbb6-8a21-5895-a193-08d9d1a311c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186409564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409557 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
